<%# locals: (vault:, vault_error:, server_address:, max_slots:, identities:) %>
<%#
  (1) THE VAULT SIGNER SET — `VaultState.signers` ++ `signers_ext`, the keys
  that sign vault ACTIONS. This is the only authority this page writes.

  ALL FIVE SLOTS ARE RENDERED, including the empty ones. An empty slot is a
  fact worth seeing: it is headroom on a five-slot program and it is what a
  reduced set leaves behind. Until this page, `read_vault_state` stopped at
  three and slots 4-5 were invisible to the app entirely.
%>
<section class="card p-4 mb-6">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-1">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Vault signer set</h2>
    <% if vault %>
      <span class="font-mono text-2xs text-muted break-all"><%= vault[:pda] %></span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <p class="text-secondary text-sm mb-3">
    <code>VaultState</code> — the keys that authorize settlement, sweeps,
    contest creation, token minting and rotation itself. Not the program upgrade
    authority; that is the Squads multisig further down.
  </p>

  <% if vault_error || vault.nil? %>
    <p class="text-sm text-warning-ink">
      The VaultState account could not be read, so this page cannot say who the
      signers are. Nothing below is safe to act on until it can.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <ol class="space-y-1.5 mb-4">
      <% slots = vault[:signer_slots] || vault[:signers] %>
      <% slots.each_with_index do |address, i| %>
        <% empty = address == Solana::SignerRotation::EMPTY %>
        <% beyond = (i + 1) > max_slots %>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2 rounded-md border px-2 py-1.5
                   <%= empty ? "border-dashed border-subtle bg-surface-alt" : "border-subtle bg-surface" %>">
          <span class="mt-0.5 w-8 shrink-0 text-3xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">
            <%= i + 1 %>
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <% if empty %>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted">
                Empty<%= " — and unreachable on the deployed program, which has only #{max_slots} slots" if beyond %>
              </p>
            <% else %>
              <%# THE PERSON FIRST, THE KEY UNDERNEATH — and the key is still
                  rendered in full. Three unbroken lines of base58 was what this
                  panel used to be, and an operator cannot tell his own wallet
                  from a stolen one by reading forty-four characters. %>
              <% server_badge = capture do %>
                <% if address == server_address %>
                  <span class="rounded bg-surface-alt px-1 py-px text-3xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">
                    This server
                  </span>
                <% end %>
              <% end %>
              <%= render "wallet_identity", address: address,
                         user: identities[address], badges: server_badge %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>

    <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-xs mb-4">
      <dt class="text-muted">Live signers</dt>
      <dd class="text-heading font-medium"><%= vault[:active_signer_count] %></dd>
      <dt class="text-muted">Slots this program has</dt>
      <dd class="text-heading font-medium"><%= max_slots %></dd>
      <dt class="text-muted">Stored <code>threshold</code> field</dt>
      <dd class="text-heading font-medium">
        <%= vault[:threshold] %>
        <span class="text-muted">— legacy, and nothing reads it for authorization</span>
      </dd>
      <dt class="text-muted">Treasury authority</dt>
      <dd class="font-mono text-2xs text-heading break-all"><%= vault[:treasury_authority] %></dd>
    </dl>

    <%# ── PAUSE IS NOT A REMEDY ──────────────────────────────────────────
        The single most important sentence on this page. An operator who
        believes pausing contains a key compromise will pause, feel safe, and
        leave the thief minting entry tokens. Verified across all 23 turf-vault
        instruction sources on `accepted`: exactly two read the flag. %>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-warning/40 bg-warning/10 p-3">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-warning-ink mb-1">
        Vault is <%= vault[:paused] ? "PAUSED" : "not paused" %> — and pausing is not a remedy
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-secondary">
        Only <code>enter_contest</code> and <code>enter_contest_with_token</code>
        check the paused flag. A paused vault still mints entry tokens, grants
        seeds and creates contests — the value-creating paths a stolen key would
        actually use. Pausing stops paying customers from entering and does not
        inconvenience a thief.
        <strong>Eviction is the only real answer</strong>, which is what the
        console at the top of this page does.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-3xs text-muted">
        Re-derive it yourself:
        <code>grep -rn 'paused' programs/turf_vault/src/instructions/</code> in
        turf-vault. Two gates, plus the three sites that set the flag.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</section>
